and help people. The link's down below.

00:09:57.480 --> 00:10:02.040
The point I'm trying to get to is that

00:09:58.680 --> 00:10:05.040
my relationship with my brand

00:10:02.040 --> 00:10:07.240
is I'm using it to fund people's dreams,

00:10:05.040 --> 00:10:09.200
your dreams. So, when you're thinking

00:10:07.240 --> 00:10:11.000
about your business, you have to think

00:10:09.200 --> 00:10:13.640
about the relationship between your

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:14.720
product and service and the consumer,

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.360
and how frankly you're going to give

00:10:14.720 --> 00:10:18.880
back to them, in my opinion. Community

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:20.120
is now the biggest opportunity in

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:21.760
business. If you think about how to

00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:24.880
disrupt the big players, let's take

00:10:21.760 --> 00:10:26.720
Amazon or even Google, they don't have

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:28.040
community. And the key thing when

00:10:26.720 --> 00:10:30.000
building a relationship and a community

00:10:28.040 --> 00:10:31.800
with your audience is not what can that

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.320
community do for you, but what can you

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:35.080
do for that community? You want your

00:10:33.320 --> 00:10:37.000
existing customers, for example, to

00:10:35.080 --> 00:10:38.720
recommend you. But to do that, you need

00:10:37.000 --> 00:10:40.960
to help them. You need to look after

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:42.520
them. You need to have a relationship

00:10:40.960 --> 00:10:44.360
with them, which means you need to make

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:46.600
yourself available or connect to the

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:49.320
audience. That's why personal brand has

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:52.200
become so important now. People are

00:10:49.320 --> 00:10:53.720
buying from me because they know me.

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:56.080
They've got to know me through my

00:10:53.720 --> 00:10:58.080
community platform, Help Bank, through

00:10:56.080 --> 00:11:00.000
social media content like this, through

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:02.200
education knowledge I'm producing. So,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.640
basically, you have to do the same, and

00:11:02.200 --> 00:11:05.280
it does require a bit of effort, like

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:06.720
any relationship. If you want to have a

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:08.120
relationship with your friends, you need

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.080
to go out with them and spend time with

00:11:08.120 --> 00:11:12.160
them. And you need to think about sales

00:11:10.080 --> 00:11:13.839
in the same way. Don't think of it, make

00:11:12.160 --> 00:11:15.480
a social media video, put it up, you get

00:11:13.839 --> 00:11:17.400
a sale, that's the end. That's why

00:11:15.480 --> 00:11:19.320
personally, Dream Brew, I'm not yet

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:20.839
selling it in supermarkets, and that is

00:11:19.320 --> 00:11:22.520
one of the biggest things in sales that

00:11:20.839 --> 00:11:24.400
I think gets overlooked. People want the

00:11:22.520 --> 00:11:25.760
sales so badly, they're willing to

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:27.960
sacrifice the relationship, and it

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:29.560
should be exactly the opposite. The next

00:11:27.960 --> 00:11:31.240
thing I want to talk about is

00:11:29.560 --> 00:11:34.360
over-deliver.

00:11:31.240 --> 00:11:36.280
Whatever you promise to do, do more than

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:38.240
people expect. I go to a restaurant in

00:11:36.280 --> 00:11:39.320
Hong Kong called Crystal Jade. It's one

00:11:38.240 --> 00:11:40.960
of my favorite restaurants at the

00:11:39.320 --> 00:11:42.960
airport in Hong Kong. And as soon as you

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:44.480
sit down in this restaurant, the first

00:11:42.960 --> 00:11:45.640
thing the waiter says to you is, "I'm

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:48.640
sorry, it's going to be about a

00:11:45.640 --> 00:11:51.280
20-minute wait." Instantly, they bring

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:52.648
you down to have a low expectation of

00:11:51.280 --> 00:11:53.120
food coming to the table.

00:11:52.648 --> 00:11:55.360
>> [music]

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:56.960
>> And then nearly every single time,

00:11:55.360 --> 00:11:59.240
within 5 minutes, the food is in front

00:11:56.960 --> 00:12:01.040
of me. They've literally created a

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:02.640
positive sales experience, because they

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:04.360
told me I wasn't going to get something.

00:12:02.640 --> 00:12:06.480
I'm happy when it came in 5 minutes,

00:12:04.360 --> 00:12:08.440
right? I was expecting it to be 30. And

00:12:06.480 --> 00:12:10.920
I think that underselling is such an

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:14.080
underrated thing in sales. Most people

00:12:10.920 --> 00:12:16.200
are trying to optimize you to sell more.

00:12:14.080 --> 00:12:17.840
I think sell less. Think about how you

00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:20.520
can bring value to people. Think about

00:12:17.840 --> 00:12:22.200
how you can undersell, not oversell, and

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:23.680
then overdeliver. Because that will

00:12:22.200 --> 00:12:25.120
encourage them to tell people about you.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:27.600
That will encourage people to come back

00:12:25.120 --> 00:12:29.680
to you. And a repeat sale is much easier

00:12:27.600 --> 00:12:32.240
than a new sale, right? Build a

00:12:29.680 --> 00:12:33.840
relationship. Make sure you overdeliver

00:12:32.240 --> 00:12:35.000
on everybody you sell to. And the final

00:12:33.840 --> 00:12:36.560
thing I'm going to teach you is probably

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:38.240
the hardest thing to actually do, cuz it

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:39.920
